<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/017F">Construction <span data-tag="017F">4.3.4.1</span>.</a> Let $X$ and $Y$ be topological spaces, and let $[0,1] = | \Delta ^1 |$ denote the unit interval. We let $X \star Y$ denote the topological space given by the iterated pushout </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  X \coprod _{ (X \times \{ 0\}  \times Y)} (X \times [0,1] \times Y) \coprod _{ (X \times \{ 1\}  \times Y) } Y. \]
</div>
<p> We will refer to $X \star Y$ as the <em>join of $X$ and $Y$</em>. </p>
